  It depends on a lot of things.  Skill limits for the role.  The Quest
Artifact.  Guaranteed first divine weapon gift?  Can the character get
to Expert with a multi-shot thrown weapon?

  Will the weapon turn to junk in Gehennom?  (Fire Brand and the Staff
of Aesculapius.)  Is the weapon junk vs the End Game Riders?
(Fire/Frost Brand and the Staff.)

  Some roles have obvious weapon choices: Knights go for long sword -
#dip for Excalibur.  Wizards go for dagger - Magicbane is first divine
gift.  Valkyries go for Mjollnir - guaranteed first divine gift.
Healers go for quarterstaff - Quest Artifact.  Caveman goes for Sceptre
of Might - Quest Artifact.  Rangers can go for bow - Quest Artifact (few
players have the temperment for it, though.)

  Some roles don't have clear cut choices.  Priests can use spears and
wish for a silver spear for Gehennom.  They can also easily get to XL 30
and cast Magic Missile for horrendous amounts of damage.

